  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Business in the Community so that they can develop guidance and expertise to help improve the coordination and effectiveness of the UK private sector when they respond to humanitarian emergencies.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Support to Business in the Community so that they can develop guidance and expertise to help improve the coordination and effectiveness of the UK private sector when they respond to humanitarian emergencies. is a component of Business in the Community: Private Sector Engagement Programme reported by FCDO with a funding type of 105 -  Humanitarian assistance and a budget of &#xA3;736,307. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Disaster prevention and preparedness.</narrative>
  </description>
